name: AML
tagline: "Anti-money-laundering typologies over a synthetic account feed - structuring, threshold crossings, smurfing, watch-list traffic, an account Risk Score, screening and Link Analysis starters"
description: "An AML function pack over two synthetic feeds (a core-banking account ledger and a party register). Needs the Professional or Enterprise edition: it carries Alert Rules, a Risk Score (Scoring & Lists), an Anomaly Model (Anomaly Detection), a screening.run Job (Screening) and a Report Template (Regulatory Reporting). Four sql.template Jobs run daily over the previous day with a look-back window: structuring (repeated cash deposits just under the reporting limit), threshold crossing (a day's cash over the limit, single or split), smurfing (many small payers into one account) and watch-list traffic (wires to a configured high-risk jurisdiction list), each with a per-account Alert Rule. The account Risk Score combines structuring, smurfing and high-risk-wire signals; its Alert Rule is created after the score's first run. The account-transfer Anomaly Model compares each account's daily outgoing transfer and wire count and value with its own history; its Alert Rule is likewise created after the model's first run. The screening Job screens the party register against two Entity Lists (aml_sanctions, aml_pep) that you create, then enable it. Link Analysis starters: an account-transfer view and the money pattern packs. Every threshold is configuration. The synthetic golden corpus lands in data/samples - copy each feed into data/inbox/<feed> to ingest. Runbooks: config/runbooks/aml-runbooks.md."
icon: heroicons_outline:shield-exclamation
contents[11]: "2 Pipelines + schemas", "4 detection Jobs (sql.template)", "4 per-account Alert Rules", "Account Risk Score + pending high-risk Alert Rule", "Account-transfer Anomaly Model + pending unusual-transfer Alert Rule", "Screening Job (disabled until the Entity Lists exist)", "Link Analysis view + 4 money pattern packs", "Illustrative STR Report Template", "3 KPIs", "Dashboard", "Runbooks"
